  "notes": "Net map: 0 = bottom rail, reached by GND 8 (bottom centre) and GND 11 (right of V-DC 9); n1 = top +5V rail (V-DC 9 plus terminal, drains of MOSFETs 10 and 5, zener top); n2 = zener bias line \u2014 left rail below zener 14, the long horizontal at y~261, gates of 10 and 13, top of V-AC 0; n3 = centre gate column (gate of 5 and 1, top of V-AC 2); n4 = mid horizontal at y~185 (source of 10, source of 5 via junction dot at (270,184), drain of 13, top lead of 7); n5 = node joining drain of 1, source of 13 and the left end of resistor 12; n6 = feedback node: gate of 7 -> down at x~352 -> right at y~261 -> down at x~398, T-joining the right end of resistor 12 at (397,311) and continuing to the gate of 6; n7 = right rail: bottom lead of 7 -> right at y~226 -> down at x~483 to the top of I-AC 4; n8 = narrow loop from the upper channel lead of 6 up to y~238 and right to the top of I-AC 3. Judgment calls: (a) the centre column at x~208 crosses the y~185 and y~261 horizontals with drawn semicircular hops (verified at 7x) \u2014 both are crossings, NOT junctions, so the column joins only gate-column members; (b) the crossing at (270,184) DOES carry a junction dot, so the source of 5 joins the mid horizontal; (c) MOSFET-P 7: top lead read as source (it faces the NMOS source node n4), bottom lead as drain \u2014 the S/D choice does not change the net grouping; (d) MOSFET-P 6: the lead running up to I-AC 3 read as drain, the grounded lead as source; (e) zener 14 terminal order is top-then-bottom as drawn (2-terminal order does not affect any metric); (f) both I-AC sources are drawn with upward arrows and their top terminal is listed first; (g) V-AC sources carry no polarity marks, so terminal order is arbitrary.",
